==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|heauily||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*keh₂p-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|hevely}}, {{m|enm|hevyliche}}, from {{inh|en|ang|hefiġlīċe|t=heavily; grievously}}, equivalent to {{af|en|heavy|-ly|id2=adverbial}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈhɛvɪli/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-heavily.ogg|a=US}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# With a great weight.
#: {{ux|en|'''heavily''' burdened}}
#: {{ux|en|She fell '''heavily''' into bed.}}
#: {{ux|en|He clomped '''heavily''' up the stairs in his boots.}}
#: {{ux|en|The great clod trod '''heavily''' on my toes!}}
#* {{RQ:Travers Cuckoo in the Nest|chapter=5|passage=The departure was not unduly prolonged.{{...}}Within the door Mrs. Spoker hastily imparted to Mrs. Love a few final sentiments on the subject of Divine Intention in the disposition of buckets;{{...}}; a deep, guttural instigation to the horse; and the wheels of the waggonette crunched '''heavily''' away into obscurity.}}
# To a [[considerable]] [[degree]], to a great extent.
#: {{ux|en|He relied '''heavily''' on the data collected by the others.}}
#: {{ux|en|Your advice still weighs '''heavily''' with me.}}
#: {{ux|en|This problem weighs '''heavily''' on my mind.}}
#: {{ux|en|He drank '''heavily'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|'''heavily''' in debt; &nbsp; '''heavily''' tattooed}}
#: {{ux|en|'''heavily''' pregnant}}
#* {{RQ:Christie Autobiography|I|4|passage=An indulgent playmate, Grannie would lay aside the long scratchy-looking letter she was writing ('''heavily''' crossed ‘to save notepaper’) and enter into the delightful pastime of ‘a chicken from Mr Whiteley's’.}}
#* {{RQ:en:New York Times|author=Miriam Jordan|title=Migrant Workers Restricted to Farms Under One Grower’s Virus Lockdown|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2020/10/19/us/coronavirus-tomato-migrant-farm-workers.html|date=2020-10-19|passage=In Virginia, gone are the weekly outings to Walmart to stock up on provisions; to El Ranchito, the Mexican convenience store, to buy shell-shaped concha pastries; and to the laundromat to machine wash '''heavily''' soiled garments.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260214215604/https://www.nytimes.com/2020/10/19/us/coronavirus-tomato-migrant-farm-workers.html|archivedate=14 February 2026}}
# In a manner designed for heavy duty.
#: {{ux|en|'''heavily''' armed soldiers; &nbsp; '''heavily''' armoured tanks; &nbsp; '''heavily''' reinforced walls}}
#* {{RQ:Allingham China Governess|chapter=14|passage=Nanny Broome was looking up at the outer wall.&nbsp; Just under the ceiling there were three lunette windows, '''heavily''' barred and blacked out in the normal way by centuries of grime.}}
# So as to be [[thick]] or [[heavy]].
#: {{ux|en|'''heavily''' built young men; &nbsp; his '''heavily''' muscled arms}}
# In a [[laboured]] manner.
#: {{ux|en|he breathed '''heavily'''}}
# Sadly.
#: {{ux|en|"It was all my fault," he replied '''heavily'''.}}

